/*!
\page page_stl1trigger StL1Trigger

\brief Level-1 software trigger data; adds a secondary "prime" trigger word to the L0 data.

\section stl1trigger_overview Overview
\c StL1Trigger extends \ref page_sttrigger with a secondary trigger word
(\c mTriggerWordPrime) that records additional condition bits evaluated by the L1
software processor (~100 µs decision time).  The inherited \c mTriggerWord is the L0
hardware word; \c mTriggerWordPrime captures L1-only refinements.

\section stl1trigger_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code
TObject
 └── StObject
      └── StTrigger
           └── StL1Trigger
\endcode

\section stl1trigger_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| UInt_t | mTriggerWordPrime | Secondary L1 trigger word |
| *(inherited)* | mTriggerWord | L0 hardware trigger word |
| *(inherited)* | mTriggerActionWord | Trigger action word |

\section stl1trigger_methods Key Methods

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `unsigned int triggerWord() const` | L0 hardware trigger word |
| `unsigned int triggerActionWord() const` | Trigger action word |
| `unsigned int triggerWordPrime() const` | Secondary L1 trigger word |
| `void setTriggerWordPrime(unsigned int)` | Set secondary L1 trigger word |

\section stl1trigger_usage Usage Example
\code{.cpp}
StL1Trigger* l1 = event->l1Trigger();
if (l1)
    cout << "L1 prime word: 0x" << hex << l1->triggerWordPrime() << endl;
\endcode

\see \ref page_sttrigger
\see \ref page_stl0trigger
\see \ref page_stl3trigger
*/
